# Bright CLI reference

The Bright CLI (`bright-cli`, npm package `@brightsec/cli`) drives scans from a shell and is the
runtime CI uses. Full docs: https://docs.brightsec.com/docs/about-bright-cli

## Install

```bash
npm install @brightsec/cli -g
bright-cli --version
```

Docker and other install methods: https://docs.brightsec.com/docs/cli-installation-guide

## Auth & environment

All commands need a token. Read it from the environment — never hardcode:

```bash
export BRIGHT_TOKEN=<your-api-key>   # scopes: bot, scans:run, scans:read
```

## Repeater (for local/private targets)

```bash
bright-cli repeater --token "$BRIGHT_TOKEN" --id "$REPEATER_ID"
```

Register a repeater in the Bright app first and copy its ID. This pulls scan traffic as outbound
connections so local targets are never exposed to the internet.

## Discovery

```bash
bright-cli discovery:run \
  --token "$BRIGHT_TOKEN" \
  --project "$PROJECT_ID" \
  --name "discovery" \
  --crawler "$TARGET_URL"
```

Poll with `bright-cli discovery:polling`. See
https://docs.brightsec.com/docs/cli-running-a-discovery

## Run a scan

```bash
bright-cli scan:run \
  --token "$BRIGHT_TOKEN" \
  --project "$PROJECT_ID" \
  --repeater "$REPEATER_ID" \
  --name "Bright scan" \
  --crawler "$TARGET_URL" \
  --smart
```

- `--smart` enables smart decisions (parameter skipping, phased detection) to optimize coverage
  and time. Recommended for most runs.
- Target a spec instead of the crawler with `--archive`/`--file` (uploaded API definition) — see
  https://docs.brightsec.com/docs/cli-running-a-scan

## Check status & retest

```bash
bright-cli scan:polling  --token "$BRIGHT_TOKEN" "$SCAN_ID"
bright-cli scan:retest   --token "$BRIGHT_TOKEN" "$SCAN_ID"   # re-verify after fixes
bright-cli scan:stop     --token "$BRIGHT_TOKEN" "$SCAN_ID"
```

Scan status polling and exit codes: https://docs.brightsec.com/docs/cli-checking-scan-status

## Configuration files

Commands can be saved as JSON/YAML/JS config and replayed. See
https://docs.brightsec.com/docs/cli-configuration-files
